<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Belz</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Belz is a small town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lviv">Lviv</a> Oblast in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>, near the Polish border. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it was one of the Cherven towns disputed between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> and Rus', the seat of a principality and from 1462 the capital of the Polish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belz-voivodeship">Belz Voivodeship</a>. From the early 19th century it was the home of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belz-hasidic-dynasty">Belz Hasidic dynasty</a>, and its large Jewish community was destroyed in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holocaust">Holocaust</a>.</p></div>
